$ mooctl cluster remove prod
error: node3: connecting to root@h3: no route to host
Pass --unreachable to remove the cluster anyway, leaving k3s on what can't be reached.
$ mooctl cluster remove --unreachable prod
Removing cluster prod:
- k3s is uninstalled from node2 (root@h2), node1 (root@h1): every app there stops, and its volumes are deleted
- node3 (root@h3) can't be reached: k3s stays there
- the cluster directory <home>/clusters/default/prod is deleted, with its secret store
This can't be undone. Type the cluster's name to remove it: Uninstalling k3s from node2...
Uninstalling k3s from node1...
Removed cluster prod
Default cluster: none
Warning: node3 (root@h3) couldn't be reached; if k3s still runs there, uninstall it there.
